.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH key 1  "key " 
.SH NAME
key \- Export or import the sync key
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBkey\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Export or import the sync key.
.PP
SUBCOMMANDS:
    agr sync key export              Print the recovery phrase
    agr sync key import [PHRASE]     Install a recovery phrase (stdin when omitted)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
key\-export(1)
Print the recovery phrase of the sync key
.TP
key\-import(1)
Import a recovery phrase on this machine
.TP
key\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
